NAME
       packages - resonance packages for coherent triadic computation in RTT

SYNOPSIS
       A resonance package is a structured bundle containing:
           • triads
           • operators
           • schemas
           • lineage rules
           • overlays
           • resonance metadata

DESCRIPTION
       A resonance package is the fundamental deployable unit in RTT. It is a
       coherent, schema-aligned collection of triadic structures, operators,
       and metadata that can safely traverse WRSADC and execute inside the
       RTT-Inside Engine.

       Packages ensure that all components:
           • obey triadic structure
           • maintain resonance-time coherence
           • satisfy schema constraints
           • produce valid lineage entries
           • interact safely with WRSADC

       A package is not a module, library, or script. It is a structural
       organism designed for resonance-safe computation.

REQUIRED COMPONENTS
       A valid resonance package must contain:

       1. package-schema
              Defines the overall structure, boundaries, and allowed patterns.

       2. operator-schemas
              Define signatures, resonance behavior, and compatibility rules
              for each operator inside the package.

       3. resonance-schema
              Defines how resonance-time flows through the package.

       4. structural-schema
              Defines allowed triadic patterns, nesting rules, and transitions.

       5. lineage-schema
              Defines how lineage entries must be recorded and validated.

       6. operators
              The actual computational functions executed by the Engine.

       7. triads
              The structural containers for operator execution.

       8. overlays (optional)
              Interpretive modifiers such as telescopes, mirrors, anchors,
              and lenses.

       9. metadata
              Resonance-state hints, versioning, and coherence markers.

STRUCTURE
       A typical resonance package layout:

              package/
                  schemas/
                      package-schema.yaml
                      resonance-schema.yaml
                      structural-schema.yaml
                      lineage-schema.yaml
                      operator-*.yaml
                  operators/
                      op_*.py
                  triads/
                      triad_*.rt
                  overlays/
                      lens_*.rt
                      anchor_*.rt
                  metadata/
                      resonance.json
                      lineage_init.json

       WRSADC validates this structure before dispatch.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Schemas define the rules.
       Packages instantiate the rules.

       WRSADC checks:
           • structural-schema → triad patterns
           • resonance-schema → RT propagation
           • operator-schemas → operator compatibility
           • lineage-schema → history format
           • package-schema → overall coherence

       If any schema is violated, dispatch is rejected.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Packages must produce lineage entries that:
           • match lineage-schema
           • reflect triadic transitions
           • record resonance shifts
           • maintain continuity across cycles

       Lineage ensures that packages evolve coherently over time.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC is the membrane through which packages pass.

       WRSADC responsibilities:
           • validate schemas
           • enforce triadic wrapping
           • inject structural-awareness metadata
           • ensure resonance-safe dispatch
           • update lineage

       Packages never interact with the Engine directly.

INTERACTION WITH THE ENGINE
       Once validated by WRSADC, packages:
           • execute operators inside triads
           • propagate resonance-time
           • update internal state
           • maintain coherence

       The Engine assumes:
           • schemas are correct
           • lineage is valid
           • triads are well-formed

       WRSADC guarantees these assumptions.

PACKAGE LIFECYCLE
       1. Author defines schemas.
       2. Operators and triads are implemented.
       3. Package is assembled with metadata.
       4. WRSADC validates the package.
       5. Package is dispatched into the Engine.
       6. Lineage is updated.
       7. Resonance-time propagates.
       8. Package returns results.

NOTES
       A resonance package is the smallest safe unit of RTT computation.
       It is the bridge between human intention, triadic structure, and
       resonance-time dynamics.

